{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This page covers common React and TypeScript problems when using TanStack Form."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"an-input-changes-from-uncontrolled-to-controlled","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An input changes from uncontrolled to controlled"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every value rendered by a controlled input must exist in form-level\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" from the first render."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    subscribed: false,\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not omit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" or rely on a field-level default. When values come\nfrom an API, render a loading state before mounting the editable form or supply\na complete fallback shape."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"a-field-value-is-unknown","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A field value is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field names and values are inferred from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":". Check that you have\nnot widened the initial object to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, unknown>"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":", or an\nunrelated union. Prefer a concrete value type:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type Profile = { firstName: string; age: number }\n\nconst defaults: Profile = { firstName: '', age: 0 }\nconst form = useForm({ defaultValues: defaults })","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For extremely large forms, split UI into typed components or scoped form/field\ngroups instead of casting each field value."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-instantiation-is-excessively-deep","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type instantiation is excessively deep"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This TypeScript error usually involves a very large recursive value shape, a\nwidely inferred union, or an unsupported composition. Reduce it to the smallest\nform that reproduces the problem, keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" concrete, and avoid\nunnecessary generic wrappers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the minimal reproduction still fails, report it in the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/form/issues","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form issue tracker"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Include\nthe TypeScript version, the form value type, and the smallest failing field."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"errors-exist-but-are-not-displayed","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Errors exist but are not displayed"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" respects the form's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" policy. Inspect\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.meta.original.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" when debugging whether validation ran but the\nissues are intentionally hidden. Also confirm that the input calls\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.handleBlur"},{"type":"text","value":" if the policy depends on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isBlurred"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"an-input-changes-from-uncontrolled-to-controlled","text":"An input changes from uncontrolled to controlled","level":2},{"id":"a-field-value-is-unknown","text":"A field value is unknown","level":2},{"id":"type-instantiation-is-excessively-deep","text":"Type instantiation is excessively deep","level":2},{"id":"errors-exist-but-are-not-displayed","text":"Errors exist but are not displayed","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThis page covers common React and TypeScript problems when using TanStack Form.\n\n## An input changes from uncontrolled to controlled\n\nEvery value rendered by a controlled input must exist in form-level\n`defaultValues` from the first render.\n\n```tsx\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    subscribed: false,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nDo not omit `defaultValues` or rely on a field-level default. When values come\nfrom an API, render a loading state before mounting the editable form or supply\na complete fallback shape.\n\n## A field value is `unknown`\n\nField names and values are inferred from `defaultValues`. Check that you have\nnot widened the initial object to `Record<string, unknown>`, `any`, or an\nunrelated union. Prefer a concrete value type:\n\n```tsx\ntype Profile = { firstName: string; age: number }\n\nconst defaults: Profile = { firstName: '', age: 0 }\nconst form = useForm({ defaultValues: defaults })\n```\n\nFor extremely large forms, split UI into typed components or scoped form/field\ngroups instead of casting each field value.\n\n## Type instantiation is excessively deep\n\nThis TypeScript error usually involves a very large recursive value shape, a\nwidely inferred union, or an unsupported composition. Reduce it to the smallest\nform that reproduces the problem, keep `defaultValues` concrete, and avoid\nunnecessary generic wrappers.\n\nIf the minimal reproduction still fails, report it in the\n[TanStack Form issue tracker](https://github.com/TanStack/form/issues). Include\nthe TypeScript version, the form value type, and the smallest failing field.\n\n## Errors exist but are not displayed\n\n`field.errors` respects the form's `errorVisibility` policy. Inspect\n`field.meta.original.errors` when debugging whether validation ran but the\nissues are intentionally hidden. Also confirm that the input calls\n`field.handleBlur` if the policy depends on `isBlurred`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: debugging\ntitle: Debugging React Usage\n---\n\nThis page covers common React and TypeScript problems when using TanStack Form.\n\n## An input changes from uncontrolled to controlled\n\nEvery value rendered by a controlled input must exist in form-level\n`defaultValues` from the first render.\n\n```tsx\nconst form = useForm({\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    subscribed: false,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nDo not omit `defaultValues` or rely on a field-level default. When values come\nfrom an API, render a loading state before mounting the editable form or supply\na complete fallback shape.\n\n## A field value is `unknown`\n\nField names and values are inferred from `defaultValues`. Check that you have\nnot widened the initial object to `Record<string, unknown>`, `any`, or an\nunrelated union. Prefer a concrete value type:\n\n```tsx\ntype Profile = { firstName: string; age: number }\n\nconst defaults: Profile = { firstName: '', age: 0 }\nconst form = useForm({ defaultValues: defaults })\n```\n\nFor extremely large forms, split UI into typed components or scoped form/field\ngroups instead of casting each field value.\n\n## Type instantiation is excessively deep\n\nThis TypeScript error usually involves a very large recursive value shape, a\nwidely inferred union, or an unsupported composition. Reduce it to the smallest\nform that reproduces the problem, keep `defaultValues` concrete, and avoid\nunnecessary generic wrappers.\n\nIf the minimal reproduction still fails, report it in the\n[TanStack Form issue tracker](https://github.com/TanStack/form/issues). Include\nthe TypeScript version, the form value type, and the smallest failing field.\n\n## Errors exist but are not displayed\n\n`field.errors` respects the form's `errorVisibility` policy. Inspect\n`field.meta.original.errors` when debugging whether validation ran but the\nissues are intentionally hidden. Also confirm that the input calls\n`field.handleBlur` if the policy depends on `isBlurred`.\n"}
